Vue, Angular, and vanilla JS.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--7cxzwRLg--/f_auto/v1776879347/posts/hZOtani2I?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-22T17:41:18.777Z"},{"id":"oNPFJnGsr","title":"I Built a Vinyl Record Interface for Music Streaming","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-built-a-vinyl-record-interface-for-music-streaming-onpfjngsr","summary":"A developer created Waxxy, a web-based music player with a vinyl record interface that simulates the experience of playing physical records. Currently supports local files and YouTube links, with Spotify and Apple Music integrations planned. The project includes a demo mode for testing without account creation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--NLNvCR_W--/f_auto/v1770699387/posts/ngRBMEMe2?_a=BAMAMiiu0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-10T09:11:34.870Z"},{"id":"kighVK09O","title":"Should we just give away the software for free?","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/should-we-just-give-away-the-software-for-free--kighvk09o","summary":"A team is considering offering their desktop software completely free with full customization, local-first architecture, and support for custom AI API keys. Their monetization strategy would rely on optional integrations with a 20% markup and paid collaboration/cloud features for teams, rather than charging for core product access. They're seeking community feedback on whether this freemium model with no forced cloud dependency is viable as a competitive differentiator.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--uzAFsM1v--/f_auto/v1770213704/posts/5HdjmQ8Fe?_a=BAMAMiiu0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-04T19:15:19.619Z"},{"id":"0PIp1F3J2","title":"HACKATHON","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/hackathon-0pip1f3j2","summary":"A team is participating in a hackathon to build an AI-driven application that accelerates insurance claims processing in Nigeria from 15-90 days to 30 minutes-1 hour using computer vision technology. The post seeks feedback and alternative ideas for the project.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-04T10:39:38.972Z"},{"id":"LKDYiJPWA","title":"Need your feedback: A Simple Tool to Discover WhatsApp & Telegram Communities - TapJoin.live","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/need-your-feedback-a-simple-tool-to-discover-whatsapp-telegram-communities---tapjoin-live-lkdyijpwa","summary":"TapJoin.live is a discovery tool for finding active WhatsApp groups, Telegram channels, webinars, and niche websites. The platform focuses on browsing and filtering communities without algorithmic feeds or noise, designed as a simple directory for joining relevant groups.","image":null,"num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-23T09:40:25.601Z"},{"id":"RDRu7TfBh","title":"Create Mockups with AI","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/create-mockups-with-ai-rdru7tfbh","summary":"Mocku.co is an AI-powered tool that generates high-resolution device mockups and video mockups in seconds. Users can upload screenshots or website URLs to create professional mockups across 6 device types with 10 environment styles, adjustable viewing angles, and chat-based editing. The platform offers 2K/4K export quality and uses a simple credit-based pricing system.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--nLg0ohMZ--/f_auto/v1759134732/posts/15Sbod7At?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-29T09:08:12.827Z"},{"id":"cZwSc0sri","title":"Introducing Iroshiki - Indexed Colors for the Web","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-iroshiki---indexed-colors-for-the-web-czwsc0sri","summary":"Iroshiki is a free, open-source CLI tool that converts ASCII color palettes (popular in Linux customization communities) into Tailwind CSS overrides and vanilla CSS rules. Built on the Bun runtime, it allows developers to easily apply unique color schemes like Nord or Catppuccin to their web projects, solving the problem of generic-looking applications while saving time on design decisions. The tool generates hundreds of documented CSS rules and includes Prism syntax highlighting support.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--UcDQBYnR--/f_auto/v1751155831/posts/azMY6OsdV?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-30T08:18:30.793Z"},{"id":"Y932IDsui","title":"Squidly - All your Github workflows in one place","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/squidly---all-your-github-workflows-in-one-place-y932idsui","summary":"Squidly is a new tool that centralizes GitHub workflow management, providing insights, monitoring, and management capabilities across repositories. The project is built with Svelte and AdonisJS and is currently seeking beta testers for feedback.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--jOSnha-e--/f_auto/v1750959950/posts/TYnSDuRWj?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-27T07:56:19.748Z"},{"id":"UD95IvcFn","title":"\"How I Built a Modern Property Management SaaS with Next.js, Prisma, and Tailwind\"","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-i-built-a-modern-property-management-saas-with-next-js-prisma-and-tailwind--ud95ivcfn","summary":"PlanniKeeper is a newly launched SaaS platform designed to streamline property management through interactive visualizations. Developed using Next.js, Prisma, and Tailwind CSS, it features intuitive interfaces for task assignment and property mapping, addressing challenges in outdated solutions.","image":null,"num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-11T20:20:10.306Z"},{"id":"HSoKY4CIq","title":"First Neovim plugin","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/first-neovim-plugin-hsoky4ciq","summary":"The post discusses the development of a Neovim plugin that functions as a natural language calculator using Snacks and numi-cli. The author has implemented features such as variable assignments and copying evaluated answers, and plans to add more before the 1.0 release. The plugin highlights the author's growing lua skills.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--xdIq34iX--/f_auto/v1739873315/posts/9Gp0yJzom","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-10T08:38:22.339Z"}],"similar_handles":["game_developers","webdev","devsquad","allshadcn","joindevops"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"f7966514-a5bb-4248-9895-4cbd51acd2c1","handle":"game_developers","name":"Game Developers","is_squad":true,"x":-9.3972,"y":9.207,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":28,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--wSF7-7I_--/f_auto/v1721427010/squads/f7966514-a5bb-4248-9895-4cbd51acd2c1","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.314239,"median_upvotes":4.5,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.017857,"avg_read_time":1.25,"tag_diversity":1.285714},"top_tags_preview":[["game-development",20],["webdev",7],["gaming",6]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.1765,9.9706],"cadence_depth":[-7.0588,-8.8088],"hype_variety":[4.25,-1.0294],"title_style":[4.0588,-6.5294]}},{"id":"94fc7a56-e6d2-403f-acd6-b988b426574f","handle":"webdev","name":"WebDev","is_squad":true,"x":-9.0193,"y":9.4576,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":27,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--3B1fh4kU--/f_auto,q_auto/v1/squads/94fc7a56-e6d2-403f-acd6-b988b426574f","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.359519,"median_upvotes":5.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.62963,"tag_diversity":2.296296},"top_tags_preview":[["webdev",9],["react",8],["javascript",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[9.7353,9.1765],"cadence_depth":[-7.1176,-8.2353],"hype_variety":[-4.0147,6.3676],"title_style":[7.75,-0.6029]}},{"id":"8a09782e-202a-450f-afda-d4dd3ae9